%N A138309 a(1)=1. a(n) = smallest integer > a(n-1) that is coprime to every (nonzero) exponent in the prime factorization of n.
%C A138309 a(10^k) for k = 1, 2, ... equals 12, 123, 1190, 11927, 119368, 1193123, 11929388, 119296655, 1192980178, 11929821437, ... . It appears that a(n) ~ c * n, with c = 1.1929..., or, equivalently, that the asymptotic density of this sequence is 1/1.1929... = 0.838... . - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 24 2026
%H A138309 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A138309/b138309.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A138309 From _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 24 2026: (Start)
%F A138309 a(n) = a(n-1) + 1 for n >= 2, if n is squarefree (A005117).
%F A138309 a(n) <= A067535(a(n-1)+1) for n >= 2. (End)
%e A138309 24 has the prime factorization 2^3 * 3^1. The smallest integer > a(23) = 26 that is coprime to 3 and 1 is 28. (27 is not coprime to 3.) So a(24) = 28.
%t A138309 a[n_] := a[n] = Module[{k = a[n-1] + 1, e = Union[FactorInteger[n][[;;, 2]]]}, While[!AllTrue[e, CoprimeQ[k, #] &], k++]; k]; a[1] = 1; Array[a, 100] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 24 2026 *)
%Y A138309 Cf. A005117, A067535, A138308, A138311.
